0227: a faster complete shader hold

The game starts only once every shader is compiled or loaded (the user's requirement); with a warm
cache that hold is CPU bound (about 1 ms per cached pipeline). Made faster without dropping any:
- Boost workers: up to all hardware threads but one, at most 16, created at startup and asleep
  unless aurora_pipeline_cache_set_boost(true) (the application boosts while the game is held for
  a batch that has not missed the cache; a compiling batch keeps the default count, the shader
  compiler needs much memory per thread). Cached pipelines stop scaling at 12-16 threads (Dawn's
  device lock).
- Dawn cache lookups on a read connection per thread (WAL readers do not block each other);
  writes, deletions and resets stay on the main connection under the mutex, readers reopen when
  its generation changes. The size-query entry is kept per thread.
- GX shader modules reused within a session (key: shader config, alpha mode, normal attachment):
  pipelines that differ only in blend/depth/cull/target share one WGSL generation and Tint parse.

